.TH DIGICARLO-GUI 1 "2026-09-23" "DigiCarlo 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
digicarlo-gui \- the DigiCarlo window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B digicarlo-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
The window does what \fBdigicarlo\fR(1) does, dressed as a cartoon Nash
Metropolitan. Waiting shots appear through the windshield, in sessions, each
print showing the date it will get. Select shots (click, shift-click,
ctrl-click, or click a session's signpost) and use the radio's preset keys:
\fBSet date\fR, \fBCamera\fR, \fBAuto\fR or \fBLeave out\fR.
.PP
The cameras and cards plugged in are in the glove box; click one to pull its
new pictures into the archive, or the road map to pull from a folder. The
horn looks for cameras again. \fBSTART\fR puts the waiting shots in the
library, and stops a job that is running.
.PP
The speedometer shows how far a job has got; its odometer counts every file
DigiCarlo has put in the library. The fuel gauge shows free space where the
library is, and the clock is the time a pull's newest shot will be dated.
.PP
It needs PyQt6 (\fBpython3-pyqt6\fR), and looks as intended with Nunito
(\fBfonts-nunito\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR digicarlo (1)
